# Always update GitHub

After finishing a user-requested change (including version bump and `npm run sync`), **commit and push to GitHub** unless the user says not to.

## Steps

1. Follow the usual git safety protocol (status, diff, log; no force-push; no amend unless allowed).
2. Stage the relevant files (never secrets: `.env`, keystores, `.wrangler/`).
3. Commit with a concise message focused on why.
4. `git push -u origin HEAD` so `origin` matches local.

## Notes

- This overrides the default “only commit when asked” preference for this repo.
- Still ask before destructive git operations (force push, hard reset, rewrite history).
- Bump `APP_VER` / `BUILD` before the commit when source changed (see `version-bump.mdc`).
